# name: test/sql/replacement_scan_paths.test
# description: The replacement scan claims markdown paths in bare FROM position on every DuckDB line
# group: [sql]

require markdown

# =============================================================================
# `FROM '<path>'` with no read_markdown() call goes through
# MarkdownReader::ReadMarkdownReplacement. Before this file the ONLY assertion
# covering that path anywhere in the suite was the decorated case in
# test/sql/markdown_vfs_paths.test, which is why a DuckDB 2.0 change that broke
# EVERY bare-FROM markdown path showed up as exactly one failing test.
#
# WHAT BROKE. DuckDB 2.0 changed ReplacementScanInput: `table_name` is now only
# the LAST dot-separated component of a QualifiedName rather than the whole
# string. So `FROM 'docs/readme.md'` arrives as table_name == "md" and
# `FROM 'x/doc.md@HEAD'` as "md@HEAD"; neither is recognisable as markdown, the
# scan declined, and the binder raised
#
#   Binder Error: No extension found that is capable of reading the file "..."
#
# The scan now asks ReplacementScan::GetFullPath(input), which rejoins the
# components and returns the original string on both lines.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A GREEN RUN HERE: on the v1.5.x line `table_name`
# ALREADY equals the full path, so every assertion below passes with or without
# that fix. This file cannot discriminate it locally -- only a v2.0 build can.
# The verifier is the `Next-line build — DuckDB v2.0` job, not `make test_release`.
# A green local run means "not regressed on 1.5.x", never "the 2.0 fix works".
# =============================================================================

# ---- The plain case: no decoration, no glob. This is the one that had no
# ---- coverage at all, and it is broken on 2.0 exactly as the decorated one is.

query I
SELECT count(*) FROM 'test/markdown/simple.md';
----
1

# ---- A glob in bare FROM position takes the scan's other arm (fs.HasGlob), which
# ---- also received the truncated name. Six markdown files live in test/markdown/.

query I
SELECT count(*) FROM 'test/markdown/*.md';
----
6

# ---- The regression case, kept here too so this file stands alone as the
# ---- replacement-scan contract. test/sql/markdown_vfs_paths.test owns the wider
# ---- decoration matrix, including the control that a decorated NON-markdown path
# ---- is still refused.

query I
SELECT count(*) FROM 'test/data/vfs_decorated.md@HEAD';
----
1

# ---- The path really is read, not merely claimed: content comes back, which is
# ---- what distinguishes "the scan fired" from "the scan fired and passed the
# ---- truncated name to read_markdown". Passing "md" through would have opened
# ---- the wrong file rather than declining, and a count alone could miss that.

query I
SELECT length(content) > 0 FROM 'test/markdown/simple.md';
----
true
